I"�<p>The Interdisciplinary Quantum Seminar is a weekly seminar run by the Brown Quantum Initiative (BQI) with the support of several Departments at Brown University. The seminar is focused on inviting Brown and external speakers work across the many fields that intersect in Quantum Science and Engineering.</p>

<p>If you would like to give a talk, please reach out to the <a href="mailto:quantum@brown.edu">BQI via email</a>! We welcome presentations from Faculty, Postdocs, and Senior Graduate Students.</p>

<p>If you’ve agreed to give a talk, please see <a href="/forSpeakers.html">this</a>.</p>

<p>To get emails about new talks and other news about Quantum Science and Engineering at Brown, you can request to join our mailing list/Google Group by following <a href="https://groups.google.com/u/1/a/brown.edu/g/brown-quantum-initiative">this link</a>.</p>

<p>We post talks on <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCqqJpga8Yx8yHioxzAg2PNw">our YouTube channel</a>.</p>

<p><strong>Time and Location</strong><br />All talks are held from <strong>noon to 1PM on Wednesdays</strong> in <strong>CIT 241</strong> unless otherwise stated.</p>

